      "repair_reason": "- [P1] The PR needs contributor action for real behavior proof plus a remaining scanner fix; ClawSweeper should not queue repair while the external proof gate is missing.; Needs attention: there are no dependency or workflow supply-chain changes, but the diff touches untrusted HTML extraction and still lets quoted attribute content steer raw-text skipping.; Review finding: [P2] Ignore raw-text openers inside quoted... (sha=52e6627c19503775db7b53bf0aaa6d7b7f75ecd6)",
      "review_summary": "The PR replaces web_fetch's regex-based HTML-to-markdown fallback with a scanner-based renderer and adds malformed-markup regression tests.\n\nPR surface: Source +539, Tests +209. Total +748 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the remaining review finding from source: the PR head checks for raw-text openers before honoring quote state in findTagEnd, so a quoted attribute containing a script-like string can still corrupt extraction. The original performance claim is source-plausible, but the PR has no real web_fetch run proving the after-fix behavior.",
      "review_followup": "- [P1] The PR needs contributor action for real behavior proof plus a remaining scanner fix; ClawSweeper should not queue repair while the external proof gate is missing.",
